<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Chimurenga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1896">1896</a>–<a href="/years/1897">1897</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Chimurenga was the uprising of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndebele-kingdom">Ndebele</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shona">Shona</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-south-africa-company">British South Africa Company</a> in 1896–1897, in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a>. Religious networks, notably the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mwari-cult">Mwari cult</a> it had patronised, played a significant role in organising Shona resistance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-chimurenga.jpg" alt="First Chimurenga" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Drawn by Frank Dadd. R.I. (died 1929) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Burnham_%26_Bonar_Armstrong_after_the_assassination_of_Mlimo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
